CS2102 IITPSx Processor Project - Claims
=========================================

This file lists the claims I make about my submission, according to the marking
scheme in the project specification.

General (applies to both programs)
----------------------------------
- asm.c and emu.c are the assembler and emulator source files, compilable with
  "gcc asm.c -o asm" and "gcc emu.c -o emu".
- Both compile with no errors under "gcc -std=c89 -pedantic".
- Both compile with no warnings under "gcc -std=c89 -pedantic -W -Wall
  -Wpointer-arith -Wwrite-strings -Wstrict-prototypes".
- The code uses consistent formatting, a sensible program structure, sensible
  names, and explanatory comments.

Assembler
---------
- Uses an internal form: the source is read once into an array of parsed lines
  (struct ParsedLine), and the two passes iterate over that internal form.
- Diagnoses label errors: duplicate labels and undefined (missing) labels.
- Produces a listing file (.lst).
- Produces an advanced listing: address, machine word, mnemonic/operand and
  label rows, with diagnostics shown on the relevant source line.
- Has a table of instruction names and expected operands (OPTAB).
- Assembles test programs (see tests/).
- Includes additional test programs for both success and failure, each with a
  brief explanation as comments within the file.
- Implements and demonstrates the SET directive (tests/test03.asm).
- Implements and demonstrates the mul and div instructions
  (tests/test04.asm, test07.asm, test10.asm, test11.asm).
- The bubble sort program assembles (tests/test05.asm).
- The bubble sort program works: it sorts its data into ascending order and
  HALTs, leaving 1 2 3 4 5 7 8 9 in memory (see tests/test05.log).

Emulator
--------
- Loads an object file (little-endian 32-bit words, from address 0).
- Produces a memory dump on normal termination.
- Executes test programs.
- Executes mul and div correctly, including detection of division by zero
  (the div instruction with A == 0 reports a runtime error and halts).
- Detects errant programs (an illegal opcode reports a runtime error and
  halts; a program counter outside memory is also reported).

Test cases
----------
- Provides multiple algorithms written in IITPSx assembly: bubble sort, summing
  a sequence, evaluating a polynomial, computing an integer mean, finding the
  minimum and maximum of an array, and computing a factorial.
- Includes tests that exercise mul and div (test07, test08, test10, test11),
  including test11 which uses both mul and div in one program.

